The `GPSD_LOG` with `LOG_PROG` level (4) would only execute if `debug >= 4`. In the fuzzer, `debug = 0`, so the logging code is not executed. But the `crc24q_check` call is always executed:

```c
if (crc24q_check(&lexer->inbuffer[idx], data_len + 6)) {
```

This reads `data_len + 6` bytes from `&inbuffer[idx]`. `data_len` can be up to 1023, so it reads up to 1029 bytes. `idx` can be up to `inbuflen - 1` where `inbuflen` is the number of bytes processed. But `inbuflen` is at most 9216 (the input size). So `idx + 1029` max is `9215 + 1029 = 10244`, which is within the 18433-byte buffer.

Wait, but `crc24q_check` reads `data_len + 6` bytes. Let me re-check:

```c
bool crc24q_check(unsigned char *data, int len)
{
    unsigned crc = crc24q_hash(data, len - 3);
    return (((data[len - 3] == HI(crc)) &&
             (data[len - 2] == MID(crc)) &&
             (data[len - 1] == LO(crc))));
}
```

It calls `crc24q_hash(data, len - 3)` which reads `len - 3` bytes, then reads `data[len-3]`, `data[len-2]`, `data[len-1]`. So it reads `len` bytes total. With `len = data_len + 6`, it reads `data_len + 6` bytes from `&inbuffer[idx]`.

Max: `idx + data_len + 6 = 9215 + 1023 + 6 = 10244`. Buffer is 18433 bytes. So no overflow.

